    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Dog Attitude is a boarding kennel for dogs, cats and ferrets at 454 chemin de l'Oratoire in Mougins, on a 3-hectare wooded estate with direct access to the departmental park. Your dog can stay in a kennel (indoor space and outdoor run, heating optional), in a fenced outdoor park of 100 to 500 sqm with a shelter, or on a mixed formula (day in the park, night in the kennel). Shared accommodation is offered only if the dogs are compatible. The site is under video surveillance and you receive videos of your dog on WhatsApp during its stay. Dog Attitude also breeds (German shepherds and Malinois) and trains.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>Published rates, per day for a sociable dog: €19 in a kennel, €22 in a park, €27 on the mixed formula; for two dogs, €35 in a kennel, €40 in a park, €54 mixed (full grid up to 6 dogs on the website). Premium food supplied by the kennel is charged extra. DHPPiL and kennel cough vaccines must be up to date, with proof sent at least 8 days before arrival. New customers go through an online pre-booking, then validated by the kennel; a one-third deposit of the stay is requested for confirmed bookings. Reception by appointment only: drop-off 8am-4pm, pick-up 8am-5pm, never on Sundays or public holidays.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if you're torn between a kennel and home boarding, consider your dog's sociability and temperament — individual kennels with a run suit dogs that need calm, while boarding at a private individual's home may suit a dog used to family life better.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Mougins sits between Cannes and Grasse, a hilltop village known for its old town and its food scene, right next to Mouans-Sartoux and the Parc de la Valmasque.</p>
